  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The increasing order of the acidity of the carboxylic acids is III $ < $ II $ < $ IV $ < $ I. In aromatic acids, electron withdrawing groups like $\\mathrm{Cl},-\\mathrm{CN},-\\mathrm{NO}_2$ increases the acidity, whereas electron releasing groups like $\\mathrm{CH}_3,-\\mathrm{OH},-\\mathrm{OCH}_3,-\\mathrm{NH}_2$ decreases the acidity.",
    "image": null
  },
